<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōnuntĭātor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōnunc-</span></b> ),
			ōris, m., id..
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who delivers any thing</i>, <i>a
				reciter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meae orationi M. Caesar actor contigit et
					pronuntiator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad M. Caes. 1, 6</span></i>
			 Mai.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In gen., <i>a relater</i>, <i>narrator</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thucydides rerum gestarum pronuntiator sincerus
					et grandis etiam fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 83, 287</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
